ymfm: the round trip without shifting a negative number

roundtrip_fp() zeroes the bits that the floating-point encoding of the chip
loses, by shifting the value right and back left again. The value is signed,
and the left shift of a negative number is undefined behaviour, which
UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer stops the program at:

  src/chips/ymfm/ymfm.h:258:29: runtime error: left shift of negative value
  -315

A multiplication says the same thing and is defined. The lines above clamp the
value to -32768 to 32767 and the exponent is at most 6, so the product is well
inside an int32_t, and the int16_t return takes it as before.

This is ADLplug-Next's own patch, applied to the submodule by
cmake/Patches.cmake when CMake configures, and it goes away once the change is
upstream.

diff --git a/src/chips/ymfm/ymfm.h b/src/chips/ymfm/ymfm.h
index 2cc2ac1..d931469 100644
--- a/src/chips/ymfm/ymfm.h
+++ b/src/chips/ymfm/ymfm.h
@@ -255,7 +255,7 @@ inline int16_t roundtrip_fp(int32_t value)
 
 	// apply the shift back and forth to zero out bits that are lost
 	exponent -= 1;
-	return (value >> exponent) << exponent;
+	return (value >> exponent) * (1 << exponent);
 }
 
 
